#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Creating-or-updating-documentation.rst:213
msgid ""
"The build runs Sphinx in parallel by default, using one worker per CPU core. "
"This is handled inside Sphinx (its ``-j auto`` option), so it behaves the "
"same on Linux, macOS, and Windows; a plain ``make -j`` does not help, "
"because each build is a single Sphinx invocation. To pin the number of "
"workers instead of auto-detecting, set ``JOBS``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Creating-or-updating-documentation.rst:219
msgid "$ make html JOBS=8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Documentation/Creating-or-updating-documentation.rst:224
